      "text": "To solve the equation \\((81)^{\\frac{1}{2}} = 3^m\\), we need to express 81 as a power of 3. We know that \\(81 = 3^4\\). Therefore, we can rewrite the left side of the equation as follows:\n\n\\[\n(81)^{\\frac{1}{2}} = (3^4)^{\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\]\n\nUsing the property of exponents \\((a^b)^c = a^{bc}\\), we get:\n\n\\[\n(3^4)^{\\frac{1}{2}} = 3^{4 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}} = 3^2\n\\]\n\nSo, the equation \\((81)^{\\frac{1}{2}} = 3^m\\) simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n3^2 = 3^m\n\\]\n\nSince the bases are the same, we can equate the exponents:\n\n\\[\nm = 2\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(m\\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
